# Skill names this pack used to have, one per line.
#
# Two things read this, which is why it is a file rather than a list inside one
# of them:
#
#   check.sh    rule 5 - a retired name written as plain prose in a skill looks
#               exactly like ordinary text, and this is what makes it catchable.
#   install.sh  removes these from a project on upgrade. A project installed
#               long ago carries its old skills forever otherwise - one had 42
#               installed, 16 of them from a predecessor pack, all visible to
#               the agent and contradicting the current workflow.
#
# **Add a name here whenever a skill is renamed or removed.** Skipping that step
# is what leaves the gap; the rules themselves are not the gap.
#
# Only names this pack itself has used. Anything else in a project's skills
# directory is the user's own and is never removed - install.sh reports it.
release
feature
implement
complete
audit
overview
techstack
onboard
adopt
brief
try
doctor
status
idea
